<title>YEMEN: Yemen doubles banks' minimum capital requirement.</title>
<headline>Yemen doubles banks' minimum capital requirement.</headline>
<dateline>SANAA 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yemen's Central Bank has decided to raise banks' minimum capital requirement to 500 million rials ($3.8 million-$5 million) from a current 250 million, a central bank official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>He said banks would have to meet the new requirement by the end of 1997.</p>
<p>Around 10 commercial banks currently operate in Yemen, one of the Arab world's poorest countries.</p>
<p>($1= varies between 100 and 130 rials)</p>
</text>
